      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `drivers/android/binder/page_range.rs`, this patch clamps the shrinker\u0027s `zap_page_range_single()` size to `usize::min(PAGE_SIZE, vma.end() - user_page_addr)`, whereas C Binder\u0027s `binder_alloc_free_page()` still passes an unclamped `16KB` `PAGE_SIZE` here.\n\n`zap_page_range_single()` requires the range to fit within a single VMA and passes `page_addr + size` to `mmu_notifier_invalidate_range_start()` while `binder_alloc_free_page()` only holds `lock_vma_under_rcu` on `vma`. Please clamp the zap size here to `min_t(unsigned long, PAGE_SIZE, vma-\u003evm_end - page_addr)` to match Rust Binder. (Also note that in `binder_free_buf_locked()`, `(buffer-\u003euser_data + buffer_size) \u0026 PAGE_MASK` rounds `vm_end` down on a partial final page, preventing a freed buffer at the end of a `1MB - 8KB` mapping from adding that final page to the shrinker freelist.)",
